+# THE SAME DEFECT ONE LEVEL UP, and it had never been given key 4's treatment. Across stores the ranker was
+# `$byStore | Sort-Object unit_price` - ONE key, over a list whose order is whatever Group-Object happened to
+# yield for that day's captures. When two stores tie EXACTLY on per-unit price nothing decided the crown, so
+# `cheapest_store`, `nomem_store` and the published `stores` order were all decided by luck and could differ
+# run to run over the very same rows.
+#
+# MEASURED on the live comparison-2026-09-17 board (572 commodities), which is the denominator this claim is
+# worth nothing without: 23 of 572 crowns are an exact multi-store tie, 26 of 572 no-membership crowns are,
+# and 132 of 572 rows carry an exact tie somewhere in their store list, so that many rows publish an
+# unreproducible store ORDER. The pair that shows it plainly is cream-of-chicken-soup and
+# cream-of-mushroom-soup: both $0.0695, both tied between Aldi and Hy-Vee, and the board crowned Aldi on one
